      "title": "r09: give the dgt_set_t a better name.",
      "message": "r09: give the dgt_set_t a better name.\n\nThe name was Dgt1_9_bcd but, in fact, it supports digits 0-9, not 1-9.\n\nThe spec listed in the initial comment appears to be missing a large\nnumber of pages - in particular, pages that might indicate what \"BCD\"\nmeans in the spec; does it mean all decimal digits or just 1-9?\n\nThat table is used for fields such as \"Liniennummer\", which I suspect\nmeans \"line number\"; I doubt that lines past line 9 start with line 11\nrather than 10, so I'm assuming BCD includes 0 here.\n\nThe renaming makes it clearer that this these fields could use\nproto_tree_add_item() with the encoding\nENC_BCD_DIGITS_0_9|ENC_BIG_ENDIAN (and neither ENC_BCD_SKIP_FIRST nor\nENC_BCD_ODD_NUM_DIG) if the encodings there could support both\nbig-endian and little-endian digit order within a byte (see !12239).\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit 884a19b8ef2799f7c44f844120fd43bbd9d3315c)",
